Update metadata of a bundle that is derived from its files, in place.

The bundle's files, checksum, title and tags are not changed. Choose what to
update with an option:

  --media   Look up the EXIF data, resolution, capture time, GPS position
            and device (camera or phone) of the bundle's images and videos,
            and store it in .bundle/MEDIA.json. This is the same file that
            bundle-python writes, and bundle-server serves it read-only.

The media scan is incremental: files whose checksum is unchanged since the
last scan are skipped, and entries of files that are no longer in the bundle
are removed. --force reads every file again.

Images: JPEG, PNG, GIF, BMP, TIFF and WebP; EXIF data from JPEG and TIFF.
Videos need ffprobe (ffmpeg) on PATH; without it they are skipped with a
warning.

Examples:
  # Look up media metadata
  bundle update /path/to/bundle --media

  # Read every file again
  bundle update /path/to/bundle --media --force

  # Machine-readable summary
  bundle update /path/to/bundle --media --json

Exit codes:
  0  success
  1  user error: no option, not a bundle
  2  system error: bundle locked, unreadable file or MEDIA.json
